{"id":"search-index","parent":"perfc-search","ord":"a0","title":"A maintained search index — stop scanning the whole vault per query","done":"2026-08-24T21:33:02-04:00","desc":"- Today a query is a substring scan over every node and every document body — work proportional to the whole corpus, on every keystroke. Folding is memoized; the scan is not.\n- The fix: an index maintained incrementally where the fold happens, so an edit updates only what changed, serving the existing substring grammar. Something in the trigram or suffix-automaton class, not a tokenizer, which would change what matches.\n- Since search moved to the server, server-only engines such as bun:sqlite's FTS5 are first-class candidates.\n- Start with a benchmark of what scanning bodies costs at realistic vault sizes, so adopting this is a number rather than a feeling.\n- Brainstorm: brainstorming/search-index.md.\n\nMerge: approved by the human at 20:14 after their manual test passed, with automatic merge granted at 20:15 — once the reviews are applied and CI is green the orchestrator merges, with nothing further to ask.","after":["search-server-side"],"created":"2026-08-19T16:46:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:23-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brainstorm":"brainstorming/search-index.md","brief":"briefs/sidx.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24T19:03:00-04:00","from":"human 2026-08-19 (PR #258 question)","merge":"merge-human","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/90460125","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/374","worktree":".worktrees/search-index"}}
{"id":"perf-sweep-2026-08-19","parent":"perfc-model","ord":"a0","title":"The O(n) sweep: whole-corpus costs still paid per edit","desc":"- The one catalogue of every place where work grows with the WHOLE VAULT (all files, all nodes, all dated history) but is paid on every small event — a keystroke, a write, a tool call. **The human's rule (2026-08-24): a vault with 1000 files should not do O(1000) work per event unless the answer inherently needs it.** Costs that scale with something else — one page, one conversation, one message — are deliberately out of scope and were pruned from this tree (the 2026-08-24 re-audit found a chat-stream quadratic family and some page-sized browser leftovers; they live in the trash if ever wanted). Already-fixed costs aren't re-listed.\n- Two audits live here: the original 2026-08-19 tree audit, and the 2026-08-24 re-audit (four parallel Opus subagents over format, server+surface, ops+chat, web client), which re-verified the originals and folded everything into the area groups below.\n- Measured anchors (2026-08-19): filter ~9.6ms/keystroke warm at 20k nodes; composer ~10ms; deriving 51.4ms/frame at 980 files (28ms of it the framework merge, dying upstream).\n- The 2026-08-24 one-line summary: **the browser is now clean — the server took over the walking.** The vault-in-browser series killed the client-side vault walks; the corpus-scaled costs now live in the server's per-tab recomputation, in git-per-write, and in the model's date/tag/validation bookkeeping.\n- **Shape: these are standing costs, not PRs.** Each leaf is one cost with evidence and a fix shape; most are one PR-sized fix on their own. A leaf graduates to a `PR:` title when it is actually dispatched — the features.olai convention — rather than being pre-carved here.\n- Rough ranking: streams-per-tab and git-per-write dominate; the agenda/date/tag costs grow with the vault's age, which is the axis this vault actually grows on; validation is paid on every single write.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:38:12-04:00","custom":{"anchors-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: the measured anchors describe a browser that no longer exists — the 51.4ms/frame derive at 980 files was answered (kolu#2187 per model-indices.md:135; #279 deleted the whole-set fold and DerivedProvider, reading.tsx is pane-scoped) and the 9.6ms/keystroke filter predates search going server-side (#270). The sweep's remaining costs are the SERVER-side children below; the browser figures should be struck or re-measured post-flip","nightly-plan":"CONVERGED 2026-08-24 ~16:40 — the orchestrator × the sweep's author (Fable, 30f81ddc), debate on the human's instruction. NIGHT 1, parallel, both auto: A list-documents-bytes (gate: listing-sizes ≡ recompute-from-body test; bench artifact on a synthetic 5k corpus) ∥ B filter-scope (gate: a NEW reusable differential harness — old walk vs new over generated corpora + the real vault, set AND order equality, an under:-through-a-mirror scenario, an edit-then-requery invalidation test; auto iff harness green, ANY divergence parks the lane; bench artifact). NIGHT 2, sequential from night-1 master: C published-maps first (gate: delta-stream equivalence — a fake subscriber replays an op corpus against old and new, identical delta sequence + identical final readAll; the identity hazard is reused shells swallowing deltas; invalidation test; alloc bench; auto iff the harness lands, else the lane SELF-DEMOTES to held and says why), then D validate-incremental as SHADOW (property test: random op sequences, incremental verdict ≡ full verdict; full stays authoritative; divergence → loud alarm; auto — behavior unchanged by construction). THE FLIPS (validate incremental-only; published drops the old path) are one-liner PRs, merge=HUMAN, gated machine-checkably on divergence-log=empty ∧ soak≥3 quiet nights. AMENDMENTS: the soak is time-bounded — flip-or-remove within 7 days, default REMOVE the shadow wiring (the harness and property test STAY — the durable artifact); divergence alarms wire into the orchestrator's morning summary and a non-empty log auto-freezes the flip. Perf numbers are reported artifacts, never CI gates"}}
{"id":"perf-dates-index","parent":"psw2-model","ord":"a6","title":"No date index: the agenda, calendar and day pages walk every node on every edit","done":"2026-08-20T04:34:18-04:00","desc":"- `datedNodes` (dates.ts line 231) flat-maps every record, with no memoization; agenda.ts line 6 says so in as many words.\n- App.tsx line 99's agenda memo re-runs whenever the derivation changes — that is, on every edit anywhere in the vault.\n- `datedDays` (dates.ts line 275) is a second, independent full walk, paid once per month navigated.\n- `datedOn` is a full walk per day-page resolution.\n- The fix has a shape this codebase already owns: an index of dated nodes on `Derived`, maintained by the patcher the way `taggedBy` is.","after":["search-server-side"],"created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:23-04:00","custom":{"merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/563c6d3d","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/278"}}
{"id":"perf-validate-incremental","parent":"psw2-model","ord":"a5V","title":"Five of six validation rules walk every record #nightly","done":"2026-08-25T02:28:08-04:00","desc":"- Of the six validation rules, only checkTargets reads an index; the duplicate-id, parent, after-acyclicity, mirror-containment and document checks each iterate the whole set (validate.ts lines 105-110).\n- Every write and every publishing probe pays for it.\n- The narrowing is named in model-indices.md line 139 — re-run the cycle check only when edges changed — and is still unbuilt.\n\nMerge: behaviour is unchanged by construction, because this ships as a shadow running alongside the authoritative validator — merge once the Grok agent's review is applied and CI is green. Switching over to it is a later, human-approved pull request, gated on an empty divergence log and at least three quiet nights of soaking, with a 7-day deadline to switch or remove.\n\nDispatched as the third item in the overnight queue, once its trigger was met: PR #382 merged and a Claude Opus slot free.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:23-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/vis.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25T00:42:00-04:00","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/3b51589b","pointers-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: substance unchanged, pointers drifted — the six rule calls are validate.ts:114-119; reportDuplicateIds:293, checkParents:312, checkAfterAcyclic:422, checkMirrorContainment:446, checkDocs:480 iterate derived.nodes; only checkTargets:387 reads derived.namedBy; the narrowing is model-indices.md:57","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/383","shadow-landed":"#383 (2026-08-25): the narrowed validator ships as a SHADOW, behaviour unchanged by construction; divergence log at $XDG_STATE_HOME/olai/validate-shadow.ndjson (one JSON line per divergence); the flip is perf-validate-flip","sweep-note":"the worktree prop was removed 2026-08-25 08:20: #383's name sweep holds every mention of the log's stem to its one spelling, and the branch/worktree shared the stem; the worktree was already deleted at merge — the pr prop carries the durable fact"}}
{"id":"perf-published-maps","parent":"psw2-server","ord":"a4","title":"Publishing rebuilds about 3× O(files) of Maps per revision #nightly","done":"2026-08-25T00:38:19-04:00","desc":"- `changeOf` builds a fresh Map of entries over every file, and is called three times per revision — for outlines, for documents and for heads — plus a copy of the broken-files map and the split of documents (published.ts lines 141, 155, 190, 228-241).\n- Entries that did not change are carried by reference, which is correct; it is the Map containers themselves that are re-minted every revision.\n\nMerge: automatic only if the delta-stream equivalence test harness lands green; otherwise the work session pauses itself and waits, per the agreed gate.\n\nDispatched as the second item in the overnight queue, once its trigger was met: the first night's work sessions merged and a Claude Opus slot free.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:23-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/pmb.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24T22:58:00-04:00","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/21a22396","pointers-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: substance unchanged, lines drifted — changeOf is published.ts:231 (entries Map at :240), call sites :177 documents / :283 outlines / :304 heads, broken-map copy :280","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/382","worktree":".worktrees/published-maps"}}
{"id":"perf-list-documents-bytes","parent":"psw2-ops","ord":"a4","title":"list_documents re-reads every .md just to report sizes #nightly","done":"2026-08-24T22:06:26-04:00","desc":"- Re-verified and reworded 2026-08-24: the old claim that it re-reads every .md file is stale — document bodies live in the in-memory set now, and nothing touches the disk. What survives is the spirit: every `list_documents` call still runs a full UTF-8 encode of every document's body just to report its size in bytes (query.ts line 1055, `bytesOf(entry.body)`) — a number the original decode already knew and threw away. The call also allocates a filtered copy of the whole document list and a fresh broken-files map each time (query.ts lines 1039-1042).\n- The fix is unchanged in shape: remember the byte count on the Document record when the file is decoded, so the listing computes nothing per call.\n\nMerge: per the agreed plan and the human's overnight word, merge once the pi agent's review is applied and CI is green. The gate is a test proving the reported sizes equal recomputed ones, plus a published benchmark on a 5,000-document corpus.\n\nDispatched overnight, on the first night, as work session A.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:23-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","brief":"briefs/pldb.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24T20:35:00-04:00","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/0c71691b","pointers-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: substance unchanged, pointers drifted ~500 lines — bytesOf encodes the whole body at documents.ts:426, paid per document at query.ts:1055; the named fix lives at documents.ts:417-424","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/375","worktree":".worktrees/list-documents-bytes"}}
{"id":"perf-filter-scope","parent":"psw2-server","ord":"a5","title":"file:/under: narrowing doesn't actually narrow the walk #nightly","done":"2026-08-24T22:55:19-04:00","desc":"- Narrowing a query by file or by subtree is a predicate applied inside the full walk, so a query scoped to one outline still visits every node in the vault; `under:` additionally calls ancestorsOf for each node (filter.ts lines 1841-1855).\n- This follows the search index: an index that serves the query grammar should serve the scopes too. The `byFile` index already covers the `file:` half.\n\nMerge: automatic only if the differential test harness is green, which is the agreed gate; any divergence pauses the work session.\n\nDispatched as the first item in the overnight queue, once its trigger was met: PR #374 merged and a Claude Opus slot freed.","after":["search-index"],"created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:23-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","brief":"briefs/fsc.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24T21:36:00-04:00","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/50530950","pointers-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: substance unchanged, pointer moved ~470 lines — inScopeOf iterates derived.nodes testing per node at filter.ts:2192-2199; scoping calls ancestorsOf per node for under: at :2316-2334","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/380","worktree":".worktrees/filter-scope"}}
{"id":"vaults-installed-deferrals","parent":"perfc-server","ord":"a2","title":"Four things PR #263 left behind","done":"2026-08-19T19:39:56-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-19 from PR #263's deferrals section, under the rule that a deferral becomes a roadmap node before the merge.\n\n1. On reconnect, the fold is re-initialised with freshly decoded entries while the store compares by value and keeps object identity — so after a dropped link, the per-record WeakMap search fold goes cold across the whole corpus. This was ruled acceptable at design time, but it is worth its own look.\n2. No browser-side benchmark measures the composition a tab actually pays any more: kolu benchmarks the merge, and patch.bench benchmarks the patch. outlines.ts carries this note in its own text.\n3. chat/state.ts's rows re-read `seq` off every key and re-sort the transcript on every frame; the transcript declares deltas, so it gained the fold too — an adoption opportunity the design never ruled on.\n4. patch.test.ts has no case for an upsert carrying no records — the life of a file arriving empty, filling, and emptying again was pinned only by the now-deleted deriving.test.ts; one case in the format suite closes it.\n\n(Deferral 6 of that pull request — the patcher's flat-list allocation — is already filed as perf-patch-residue; deferrals 3 and 7 were deliberate and reasoned.)","created":"2026-08-19T18:11:31-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:23-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #263 deferrals","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/1cc4cd65","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/265"}}
{"id":"reconnect-seed-upstream","parent":"perfc-server","ord":"a1","title":"Upstream: kolu should seed a reconnect, so olai's stopgap can go","done":"2026-08-20T10:28:07-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-19 at PR #265's merge, under the rule that a deferral becomes a roadmap node before the merge.\n- olai PR #265 fixed the cold start of the fold after a dropped link by seeding it from the store (a helper called seedOf), and calls itself a stopgap in as many words.\n- kolu already has `syntheticSnapshot` and already uses it to seed a registration made mid-stream; one line upstream on the wire-snapshot path would make initialisation hand back the store's own objects.\n- When that lands: olai deletes seedOf, its test, and the benchmark's wire arm.\n- The author's benchmark, for scale: one search after a dropped link took 29.9 ms when seeded from the wire versus 16.3 ms when held by the store (980 files, 21,552 records).\n- Done 2026-08-20. The olai half went first, for a different reason: PR #279 — the big switch-over — deleted seedOf, its test and the benchmark arm along with the rest of the browser-held vault. The kolu half is kolu PR #2189, merged as 2d72179a5 by the Claude Opus agent, with the Grok agent raising no objection after an out-of-tree mutation check: the wire-snapshot path now seeds every fold from `syntheticSnapshot()` after `applySnapshot`, so a fold gets the store's own objects whether it registered before or after the snapshot — one answer, pinned by a reconnect-identity test. Downstream checked: drishti and odu register no folds, so no paired pull request was needed.","created":"2026-08-19T19:39:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:13:23-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #265 deferral 1","repo":"repo-kolu"}}
{"id":"vault-in-browser","parent":"perfc-server","ord":"a0","title":"The browser holds the whole vault — stops scaling at thousands of documents","done":"2026-08-20T07:26:38-04:00","desc":"The human's ruling, 2026-08-19, in their words: this is not a 'good' thing — when we have 1000s of .md files it will start to suck. To resolve.\n\n- **The target, ruled**: the browser can at most only have the CURRENT PAGE's data in memory — never the whole vault.\n- **Design**: brainstorming/vault-in-browser.md (Fable, 2026-08-19; iterated with the human in the designer's terminal). The wire goes page-scoped; the format layer does not move; the browser's half of the fold dies.\n- **Staging law, the human's words**: \"I won't accept 'The ugly coexistence'. Every PR must be self-contained, leaving no legacy code.\"\n- **The settled sequence — ten PRs**: (1) search-server-side [first; already its own node] · (2) tag vocabulary · (3) transcript id-marking · (4) calendar dots + agenda count · (5) pins · (6) fold re-filing · (7) read_node gains blocked-status · (8) the date index · (9) the offline overlay — 2–9 in any order, each complete on its own merits with its local walk deleted in the same diff · (10) LAST: the big one — the new wire member, all seven routes flipping to it, the whole-set machinery deleted, one diff, with the parity test and the before/after byte measurement riding it. PR 10 cannot be split: the law forbids both shipping the member unused and flipping routes one at a time; PRs 1–9 exist to shrink it.\n- **Both UX decisions RULED** (doc §5): (a) navigation may round-trip, cache nothing; (b) a dead wire freezes the app under an offline overlay.\n- #204 deflated one part; this replaces the model itself. Lanes dispatch on the human's word.","created":"2026-08-19T19:56:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:43-04:00","custom":{"done-story":"ALL TEN merged in one night (2026-08-19→20): #270 search, #271 transcript ids, #272 tags, #273 calendar, #274 pins, #275 blocked-status, #276 refile, #277 the offline overlay, #278 the date index, #279 THE FLIP (7e208f77) — the browser holds only the current page's data; first frame 1,679→135 kB (12×); the whole-set fold, DerivedProvider and seedOf are gone; parity property-tested per route before the old path died","from":"the human's ruling 2026-08-19","overnight":"APPROVED by the human 2026-08-19 via question tool: after the e2e cleanup merges, all TEN PRs run overnight on Opus, 3 lanes at a time (PR 1 first alone since 2–9 wait on it; PR 10 last, gated on 2–9) — every one auto-merges on its own green pipeline, none held for morning; deferrals fold into the same PR unless a strong reason is argued"}}
{"id":"search-server-side","parent":"perfc-search","ord":"a1","title":"Search goes entirely server-side — the first step out of vault-in-browser","done":"2026-08-20T00:52:43-04:00","desc":"Ruled by the human 2026-08-19: the browser's search boxes (⌘K palette, header box, filter bar) stop scanning the local copy and query the server instead.\n- Engineering that comes with it: per-keystroke round-trips need debounce + stale-response cancellation; results arrive async where they were sync; offline/flap behavior changes and must be decided, not inherited.\n- What it unlocks: the search index no longer needs to run in the browser — server-only shapes (bun:sqlite FTS5 trigram) become first-class candidates instead of a compromise. brainstorming/search-index.md rewrites on this premise.\n- The one-matcher rule bends, not breaks: whatever engine answers, ranking and the grammar stay defined in one place, and an oracle test pins server answers to the reference matcher.","see":["vault-in-browser"],"created":"2026-08-19T19:56:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:43-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human's ruling 2026-08-19","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/1954f3c3","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/270"}}
